Read a non-blocking frontend's microphone for the whole frame

LibRetroInput::PollMicrophone reads 128 samples once per retro_run, a size
chosen so RetroArch's blocking CoreAudio read returns in one pass. The 3DS mic
service consumes the samples at the game's rate, which from a 48 kHz frontend
is about 800 a frame: with one read per frame the game received a sixth of its
signal, and between reads its buffer did not advance.

This keeps reading while each read comes back full, up to the sample ring's
4096-sample capacity. A frontend that has fewer samples returns a short read
and the loop ends, so RetroArch sees the one read it saw before. A frontend
whose read never blocks and always has a frame's worth (the iOS host's
simulated blow) now hands the game a frame's worth per frame.

--- a/src/audio_core/libretro_input.cpp
+++ b/src/audio_core/libretro_input.cpp
@@ -229,12 +229,25 @@
     // without an explicit barrier.
     std::atomic_thread_fence(std::memory_order_acquire);
 
-    int samples_read = impl->mic_interface->read_mic(impl->mic_handle, impl->read_buffer.data(),
-                                                     static_cast<size_t>(impl->read_buffer.size()));
+    // One read per frame brings 128 samples, while the game consumes about 800
+    // a frame (48 kHz). Keep reading while the frontend fills the whole buffer,
+    // up to the ring's capacity: a frontend whose read never blocks (an iOS
+    // host's) hands over a frame's worth this way. A frontend that has less
+    // returns a short read and ends the loop, so one read stays one read there.
+    for (std::size_t total = 0; total < 4096;) {
+        int samples_read = impl->mic_interface->read_mic(
+            impl->mic_handle, impl->read_buffer.data(),
+            static_cast<size_t>(impl->read_buffer.size()));
 
-    if (samples_read > 0) {
+        if (samples_read <= 0) {
+            break;
+        }
         impl->sample_buffer.Push(
             std::span<const s16>(impl->read_buffer.data(), static_cast<size_t>(samples_read)));
+        total += static_cast<std::size_t>(samples_read);
+        if (static_cast<std::size_t>(samples_read) < impl->read_buffer.size()) {
+            break;
+        }
     }
 }
 
